  "summary": "Passive native Godot PaymentCo preview with five departments, ten humans/three agents, directed links, actual information motion/statuses, work/proposal assurance and event feed. Independent source-pinned native run displays matching Python IDs/statuses and captures viewport. Read-only UI, default until-close lifetime and owned cleanup.",
  "reviewer": "Worker self-review followed by root operator independent code, regression, live runtime and visual inspection",
  "review_notes": "Codex worker self-review examined AE-020 source, public graph projection, protocol, independently reviewed tests/real loopback measurement and passing entry hashes. Archived predecessor receipt and pre-edit shared docs. Focused smoke red fails on missing scripts; final smoke passes original IDs/order, atomic rejection, passive render time, terminal facts, resnapshot bounds and refresh-cursor race. Real Python fixture regenerates identically; complete Godot headless playback reports the final Python snapshot ID, 13 actors, three proposals and received/lost states. Four Python tests pass, including explicitly mocked cleanup; initial mock PID failure retained. Required import/probe/diff checks and receipt checker are recorded, while actual socket/display failures remain visible and no live/visual pass is invented. Receipt outcome pass means bounded source/self-review readiness under independent-validation semantics; operator must validate the actual live desktop milestone. Shared ledger outside scope was not edited; review.md is the scoped ledger. No manifest/checker edits, controls, synthetic participants, successor execution or publication. Local delivery remains failed; operator hash-reviewed delivery retry is required before successor recommendation. Original self-review/limitations are preserved in the archived receipt. Root independently validated all original bindings, reproduced and fixed scroll and historical-send presentation defects, corrected a resync test setup, and retained raw native V-sync failures. Headless live state passed; disabled V-sync enabled actual native update/capture. Project caps presentation at 60 FPS with V-sync off. A final source-pinned native run completed all three real jobs and verified 13 actor IDs, three proposal IDs and received/lost statuses against Python. Viewport inspected; no desktop/private world captured. Default until-close cleanup and finite-diagnostic early-exit rejection passed six bootstrap cases; 37 transport cases and headless import/probe/fixture replay pass. No management/FPS/player/calibration gate claim. Original protected-Git delivery failure is historical; root hash-reviewed controller retry supplies separate local delivery. First operator delivery retry correctly failed because root evidence collection bound ignored bytecode caches that were not transferable source artifacts. Original receipt/cache bytes and failed attempt preserved; corrected to source/evidence bindings only. No acceptance command or code changed.",
